[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.satisfies.boolean_match] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: satisfaction outcomes over expanded comparator alternatives Witness: uncovered_slugs='semver.satisfies.boolean_match,semver.parse_range.comparators_and_prefixes'. The range scenarios assert only the echoed raw_text of wildcard, caret, tilde, hyphen and union expressions; the contracted satisfaction postcondition over their comparator expansions is never evaluated, so neither matching nor non-matching candidate versions are tested for wildcard conjunctions, for the !=, <, <= and > relational outcomes, for caret boundaries past the first non-zero component, for tilde upper bounds, or for hyphen conjunctions whose upper bound is a full semantic version; boolean_match therefore remains unverified for these contracted grammar forms.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.parse_range.malformed_syntax] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: wildcard prefix edge forms and hyphen validation Witness: uncovered_slugs='semver.parse_range.malformed_syntax,semver.parse_range.bare_partials_prohibited,semver.parse_range.hyphen_ranges'. Wildcard targets composed solely of a wildcard identifier (bare '*'/'x' forms under ==, !=, >, <, <=, ^ and ~) and wildcard expressions with more than three components or with a numeric component following a wildcard are unexercised; hyphen expressions whose token arity is not exactly two bounds around the standalone '-', or whose lower bound is a bare partial version lacking a wildcard, and standalone relational/prefix operator tokens lacking an operand, all contracted to raise InvalidRangeError, are never evaluated, so the malformed_syntax closure beyond blank, comma, empty-union and bare-partial single-comparator inputs stays unverified.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.compare_precedence.prerelease_ordering] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: prerelease identification and build metadata grammar Witness: uncovered_slugs='semver.compare_precedence.prerelease_ordering,semver.compare_precedence.build_metadata_ignored,semver.satisfies.prerelease_filter'. Two differing non-numeric prerelease identifiers are never ordered ASCII-lexicographically; a range that explicitly names a prerelease identifier sharing the candidate's major, minor and patch is never evaluated with include_prerelease False, so the contracted explicit-target exemption and the prerelease_inequality boundary case are unverified; build metadata is entirely absent from the scenarios, since no '+build' version is parsed and no precedence comparison between versions differing only in build metadata occurs, leaving build_metadata_ignored unexercised.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.solver.unsatisfiable_conflict] [viol:pret_cov.collaborator_seeding_deficit] Facet: repository seeding for transitive conflict detection Witness: uncovered_slugs='semver.solver.unsatisfiable_conflict'. The conflict scenarios cover unregistered roots, mutually contradictory root constraints, and a declared dependency whose target has no release satisfying it, but never the contracted case where a release's declared transitive dependency contradicts the release already selected for that dependency after it was assigned; that unsatisfiable_conflict outcome must raise ResolutionConflictError with conflicting_packages naming both the requiring and the contradicted package plus a derivation explanation, and the scenario that reaches it is still absent.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_pretense.py: Extended the conforming vocabulary used by the implementation scenario suite: added bare-wildcard prefix forms (==*, !=*, >*, <*, <=*, >=*, bare *, ^x, ~x) to the range-expression domain and added beta 1.0.0/2.0.0 plus omega 1.0.0 (declared dependency beta >=2.0.0) to the release sample domain, enabling deterministic coverage of wildcard prefix parsing and of a transitive contradiction against an already-assigned package selection. All additions are valid inputs with no model exception branch, so gated rule execution stays raise-free.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Expanded deterministic scenario coverage: added satisfaction outcomes over expanded comparator alternatives (wildcard conjunctions for 1.x/1.2.x/*, !=/< /<=/> relational outcomes, caret boundaries past the first non-zero component, tilde upper bounds, hyphen conjunctions with wildcard and full-version upper bounds, and union alternatives); added prerelease ASCII lexicographic ordering between differing identifiers, numeric-below-alphanumeric ranking, longer-sequence ranking, '+build' parsing/formatting and build-metadata-ignored precedence, explicit-prerelease-target exemption and prerelease inequality boundaries; extended range grammar with bare-wildcard prefix forms and malformed closure (standalone operator tokens, wrong hyphen arity, bare-partial hyphen lower bound, >3-component and numeric-after-wildcard forms raising InvalidRangeError); and added a transitive contradiction after assignment (omega requires beta >=2.0.0 while beta is pinned to ==1.0.0) asserting ResolutionConflictError names both packages with a derivation explanation.
