[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.parse_range.comparators_and_prefixes] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: caret boundaries with all zero components Witness: uncovered_slugs='semver.parse_range.comparators_and_prefixes,semver.satisfies.boolean_match'. The caret scenarios exercise only boundaries whose first non-zero component lies in major, minor or patch; a caret range over the all-zero full version and caret ranges over wildcard expressions whose every specified component is zero ('0.x', '0.0.x') are never parsed or evaluated, so the contracted expansion for a boundary that has no non-zero component is unverified and no candidate version is tested for inclusion or exclusion against those upper bounds.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.parse_range.comparators_and_prefixes] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: wildcard relational bounds with numeric prefix Witness: uncovered_slugs='semver.parse_range.comparators_and_prefixes,semver.satisfies.boolean_match'. Only the bare-wildcard form of the strict and inclusive upper comparators is exercised; '<' and '<=' applied to a wildcard expression carrying a numeric prefix are never parsed or evaluated, so the contracted relational semantics that excludes everything at or above the wildcard's lower bound, and everything at or above its exclusive upper bound, remain unverified with no included or excluded candidate versions tested for those two wildcard upper-comparator forms.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: [slug:semver.parse_range.malformed_syntax] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: hyphen upper bound grammar violation Witness: uncovered_slugs='semver.parse_range.malformed_syntax,semver.parse_range.hyphen_ranges'. Hyphen scenarios cover a full-version upper bound and wildcard bounds, and the malformed lower-bound case is exercised, but a hyphen range whose upper bound is neither a full semantic version nor a wildcard expression is never evaluated; the contracted malformed_syntax outcome requiring InvalidRangeError for that symmetric upper-bound violation remains unverified.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_pretense.py: Extended the conforming range-expression domain with the caret all-zero boundary forms (^0.0.0, ^0.x, ^0.0.x) and numeric-prefixed wildcard relational upper-bound forms (<1.x, <=1.x, <1.2.x, <=1.2.x) so the deterministic scenario suite can parse and satisfy-evaluate them through the checked transitions; all additions are valid, exception-free expressions so gated rule execution remains raise-free.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Closed remaining caret/wildcard/hyphen grammar coverage: added parse coverage for caret boundaries with no non-zero component (^0.0.0, ^0.x, ^0.0.x) and for numeric-prefixed wildcard relational upper bounds (<1.x, <=1.x, <1.2.x, <=1.2.x), added satisfaction inclusion/exclusion outcomes for those expansions (caret all-zero upper bounds; '<' excluding everything at or above the wildcard lower bound; '<=' excluding everything at or above the wildcard exclusive upper bound), and added the symmetric malformed hyphen upper-bound probes (1.0.0 - 2, 1.0.0 - 2.0, 1.0.0 - latest) asserting InvalidRangeError.
